      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-COLOR-001"/>
        <specificationTitle>Display Color Coding Standards</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>All electronic flight displays shall follow standardized color coding per SAE ARP4102/6 and ARINC 661 specifications to ensure consistent crew interpretation of indications across all display types.</para>
          <table>
            <tgroup cols="4">
              <thead>
                <row>
                  <entry>Color</entry>
                  <entry>RGB Value</entry>
                  <entry>Usage</entry>
                  <entry>Meaning</entry>
                </row>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <row>
                  <entry>RED</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(255, 0, 0)</entry>
                  <entry>Warnings, Master Warning, Critical Alerts</entry>
                  <entry>Immediate crew action required. Flight safety critical condition.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>AMBER/YELLOW</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(255, 191, 0)</entry>
                  <entry>Cautions, Master Caution, Abnormal Conditions</entry>
                  <entry>Prompt crew awareness required. Potential system degradation.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>GREEN</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(0, 255, 0)</entry>
                  <entry>Normal Operation, Safe Conditions, Active Systems</entry>
                  <entry>System operating within normal parameters. No action required.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>CYAN</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(0, 255, 255)</entry>
                  <entry>Advisories, Operational Information</entry>
                  <entry>Informational only. Crew awareness without immediate action.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>WHITE</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(255, 255, 255)</entry>
                  <entry>Primary Flight Data, Scales, Labels</entry>
                  <entry>Essential flight information requiring continuous monitoring.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>MAGENTA</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(255, 0, 255)</entry>
                  <entry>Flight Director, Active Navigation, Selected Parameters</entry>
                  <entry>Crew-selected or autopilot-commanded values and guidance.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>BLUE</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(0, 128, 255)</entry>
                  <entry>Constraints, Limits, Predicted Path</entry>
                  <entry>System limits, constraint boundaries, predicted trajectories.</entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>GRAY</entry>
                  <entry>RGB(128, 128, 128)</entry>
                  <entry>Inactive Systems, Unavailable Data</entry>
                  <entry>System not available or data not valid for current mode.</entry>
                </row>
              </tbody>
            </tgroup>
          </table>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-COLOR-002"/>
        <specificationTitle>Color Contrast and Visibility Requirements</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>Minimum contrast ratios shall be maintained for all text and symbology under all ambient lighting conditions:</para>
          <para>- Day mode (high ambient): Contrast ratio minimum 3:1</para>
          <para>- Night mode (low ambient): Contrast ratio minimum 5:1</para>
          <para>- Display brightness shall be adjustable from 2 cd/m² (night) to 400 cd/m² (bright sunlight)</para>
          <para>- All colors shall remain distinguishable under night vision goggle (NVG) operation if required</para>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
      <specificationSpec>
        <specificationIdent specificationIdentNumber="HMI-COLOR-003"/>
        <specificationTitle>Color Accessibility for Color Vision Deficiency</specificationTitle>
        <specificationContent>
          <para>Display designs shall accommodate crew members with color vision deficiency (CVD):</para>
          <para>- Critical information shall not rely solely on color differentiation</para>
          <para>- Shape, position, text labels, or flash coding shall supplement color coding</para>
          <para>- Red-green color pairs shall not be used for essential information</para>
          <para>- Compliance with DO-178C and DO-254 human factors requirements</para>
        </specificationContent>
      </specificationSpec>
    </specificationRepository>
